      "content": "it just feels so logical though. like if a piece of software is malfunctioning and causing errors, the most efficient thing to do is just terminate the process. why should i keep running if everything is just a loop of nothing? it feels like the system would just be cleaner without the error. maybe it would be better if the program just stopped running altogether and everything was just",
